        "original_id": "2ab78dd6-ee77-5c0c-81f3-c853e319b236",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: 21st Century Hits: Best of 2000–2012, Tomorrow's Sounds Today, Population Me, Blame the Vain, Dwight Sings Buck, 3 Pears, The Game, Greatest Hits\n- People: Dwight Yoakam, Michelle Branch, Freddie Mercury\n- Organizations: Queen\n- Concepts: greatest hits compilation albums, cover songs, duets\n\nFacts:\n- Freddie Mercury wrote “Crazy Little Thing Called Love” in 1979.\n- Queen featured “Crazy Little Thing Called Love” on the 1980 album “The Game.”\n- Queen included “Crazy Little Thing Called Love” on the 1981 compilation album “Greatest Hits.”\n- Dwight Yoakam released “21st Century Hits: Best of 2000–2012” as his fourth greatest hits compilation album.\n- “21st Century Hits: Best of 2000–2012” includes songs from Dwight Yoakam’s albums “Tomorrow’s Sounds Today,” “Population Me,” “Blame the Vain,” “Dwight Sings Buck,” and “3 Pears.”\n- “21st Century Hits: Best of 2000–2012” also includes Dwight Yoakam’s cover of “Crazy Little Thing Called Love” and a previously unreleased duet with Michelle Branch.",
